{title: Just As I Am}
{artist: Charlotte Elliott / William B. Bradbury}
{genre: Hymn, Communion}
{flow: Response}
{style: Traditional}
{key: D}
{tempo: 66}
{time: 3/4}
{hymnal: 새찬송가 282장}
{title_ko: 큰 죄에 빠진 날 위해}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Just as I [D]am, without one [G]plea
But [D]that Thy blood was [A]shed for me
And [D]that Thou bidd'st me [G]come to Thee
O [D]Lamb of [A]God, I [D]come, I come
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Just as I [D]am, and waiting [G]not
To [D]rid my soul of [A]one dark blot
To [D]Thee whose blood can [G]cleanse each spot
O [D]Lamb of [A]God, I [D]come, I come
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Just as I [D]am, though tossed a[G]bout
With [D]many a conflict, [A]many a doubt
Fightings and [D]fears within, [G]without
O [D]Lamb of [A]God, I [D]come, I come
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
Just as I [D]am, poor, wretched, [G]blind
[D]Sight, riches, [A]healing of the mind
[D]Yea, all I [G]need in Thee to find
O [D]Lamb of [A]God, I [D]come, I come
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
Just as I [D]am, Thou wilt re[G]ceive
Wilt [D]welcome, pardon, [A]cleanse, relieve
Be[D]cause Thy promise [G]I believe
O [D]Lamb of [A]God, I [D]come, I come
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
Just as I [D]am, Thy love un[G]known
[D]Has broken every [A]barrier down
Now to be [D]Thine, yea Thine a[G]lone
O [D]Lamb of [A]God, I [D]come, I come
{end_of_verse}
